#
# Fell, search and rescue coordination: L2, slot 253. The search grid and
# its sectors, which sector to search next, the sightings and the leads
# they give, the crews' shifts and check-ins, callout claims and the
# casualty records, over maps and places (place.here, place.list,
# place.add), radio messages (ehop.bands, ehop.seal, ehop.open,
# harmonic.encode, harmonic.decode, freight.pack), the team room
# (chat.post, chat.feed, pspace.post) and the Hoard (files.read,
# files.write). See fell_model.h FM1-FM9 and fell_rules.h FR1-FR8.
#
# Life-safety: advisory and human-approved. Every priority, lead and
# overdue crew is a suggestion for the incident commander, who decides.
# Fell never calls emergency services or anyone by itself, transmits
# nothing (zxvd has no radio method; a sealed or line frame is handed to
# the view) and infers nothing clinical: a triage category and a medical
# note are kept as the team recorded them. Every change to kept state (the
# incident, the grid, a sector, a crew, a claim, a casualty, the file, a
# post, sharing, the radio bands) is made only on the owner's word
# (owner_confirmed). The sealed radio path is for private bearers only,
# never amateur radio (docs/P2P_PROTOCOL_TWINS.md P13; Aerie's AR5 refuses
# it). Callout claims are records for the owner to settle; Fell pays
# nothing.
#
# Composed, not written again (four uses of ZXAPP_USES 8; its own 9 logic
# lines and its parts' are inside ZXAPP_LOGIC_MAX 128, tests/fell_zxapp.inc
# counts them; every part carries version 1.0.0 and its provides lines):
# a place on the globe is waymark.place_ok (Waymark checks every place it
# keeps, and the grid's corner and a sighting's place are kept places); a
# line frame's tag is aerie.frame_tag, split back by its inverse
# (aerie_tag_split), and whether a radio message fits its Endian Hopping
# band is aerie.band_fits; where the command post is may be posted to the
# team only when watchfire.place_share_ok holds, and a casualty's medical
# note fits watchfire.medical_id_ok (Watchfire's fields 1..6, as typed);
# "may I post here" is commons.room_post_ok.
#
# The task's slot 253 is no matrix layer (zxapp.c M1: 0..144); an L2 app
# sits on the layer of its part that is outermost in MATRIX_ORDER.tsv:
# Watchfire (place 129, layer 143), past Aerie (59) and Commons (16);
# Waymark is a wave 0 app, nearer the core.
#
# Witness pairs are of one kind (zxapp.c run_one B3). Sector priority is a
# number, Trebago and KRON: Trebago refuses a poa or coverage outside
# 0..10000, where KRON answers it: held. Crew safety is a truth over two
# fields, each against its own range, which Eve holds; KRON witnesses it,
# reading a minute count below 0 as safe where Eve refuses it: held.
#
# Later layers use the team room and the casualty records (Relume, Vesper,
# Sightline, Landfall), crew safety (Celesta, Tephra) and sector priority
# (Tephra, and a later layer's search), so those three are registered in
# CONCEPTS.tsv with Fell as owner. Kept in C: the four-valued join of
# disagreeing sightings (lpres_kjoin, lpres_disjoin; FR8), zxvd's answers,
# the file's lines and the notices' words.
#
# Planned (no runtime yet): Prolog owns rules and searching for every
# answer that fits, so it waits on sector_unsearched, the board's search
# filter. Go is on the task's planned line but already runs (LANGUAGE_FIT
# go) and owns concurrency and messaging; Fell's messages are Aerie's and
# Commons's, it decides nothing of that kind, so it has no Go block and no
# pending line (a pending line is refused for a running language).
zxapp 1
id     fell
name   Fell
version 1.0.0
slot   253
layer  L2
matrix 143
icon   icons/l2/253-fell.svg
budget 233
needs  location
needs  peers
needs  net
needs  fs.read
needs  fs.write
needs  notify
model  apps/fell_model.c
use    waymark 1     # @logic.waymark_place_ok
use    aerie 1       # @num.aerie_frame_tag @logic.aerie_band_fits
use    watchfire 1   # @logic.watchfire_place_share_ok @logic.watchfire_medical_id_ok
use    commons 1     # @logic.commons_room_post_ok
# what it exports, so apps built from it can use them too (C1)
provides waymark.place_ok truth lat lon
provides aerie.frame_tag num sync shell trunk
provides aerie.band_fits truth bytes frame
provides watchfire.place_share_ok truth started optin listed placeok
provides watchfire.medical_id_ok truth field bytes stamp
provides commons.room_post_ok truth member joined enabled

# Each sector's search priority (FR1, critical): probability of area less
# what the searches have covered, x10000, summing to exactly 10000; a
# suggestion for the incident commander. FORTRAN as Trebago, APL as KRON.
provides sector_priority num poa cov
logic    trebago sector_priority apps/blocks/fell/priority.tb
logic    kron    sector_priority apps/blocks/fell/priority.kron

# One crew safe (FR2, critical): shift at most 12 hours, last check-in at
# most 60 minutes ago; a crew not safe is overdue, raised for the
# commander. Ada as Eve, APL as KRON.
provides crew_shift_safe truth worked since
logic    eve  crew_shift_safe apps/blocks/fell/crew.eve
logic    kron crew_shift_safe apps/blocks/fell/crew.kron

# The sector grid (FR3): a point's sector from its offsets east and north
# of the grid's corner. APL as KRON.
provides search_grid_sector num east north cell cols
logic    kron search_grid_sector apps/blocks/fell/grid.kron

# The board's filters as K queries (FR4, FR5): sectors searched under the
# bar, and the sightings between two times. APL as KRON.
provides sector_unsearched truth cov bar
logic    kron sector_unsearched apps/blocks/fell/unsearched.kron
pending  Prolog sector_unsearched

provides sightings_between num stamp from to
logic    kron sightings_between apps/blocks/fell/sightings.kron

# A callout claim (FR6): crew hours and mileage in minor units, refused on
# overflow. COBOL as Sutra.
provides callout_claim num hours rate miles permile
logic    sutra callout_claim apps/blocks/fell/callout.sutra

# The casualty tree (FR7): ^ZXFELL(incident, casualty) = sector ^ triage
# ^ stamp. MUMPS as MYRA.
provides casualty_record_ok truth incident casualty sector triage stamp
logic    myra casualty_record_ok apps/blocks/fell/casualty.myra

# Its own proof (zxapp.h K1): each entry at its edges, and where its languages disagree
check sector_priority poa=5000,3000,2000 cov=0,5000,0 = 5882,1765,2353
check sector_priority poa=5000,5000,0 cov=10000,0,0 = 0,10000,0
check sector_priority poa=5000,5000 cov=0,10001 = both
check sector_priority poa=10001,0 cov=0,0 = both
check crew_shift_safe worked=0,720,721,300,300,0 since=0,60,0,61,60,0 = true,true,false,false,true,true
check crew_shift_safe worked=100,-1 since=0,0 = both
check crew_shift_safe worked=100,100 since=0,-1 = both
check search_grid_sector east=0,999,1000,2500,0,2999 north=0,0,0,1500,2999,999 cell=1000,1000,1000,1000,1000,1000 cols=3,3,3,3,3,3 = 1,1,2,6,7,3
check sector_unsearched cov=0,4999,5000,10000 bar=5000,5000,5000,5000 = true,true,false,false
check sightings_between stamp=51000,51120,50000,52000,51200 from=51000,51000,51000,51000,51000 to=51200,51200,51200,51200,51200 = 3
check callout_claim hours=0,10,999,0,12 rate=0,2500,999999,0,1800 miles=0,40,0,9999,85 permile=0,45,0,9999,45 = 0,26800,998999001,99980001,25425
check casualty_record_ok incident=1,999999,1000000,1,1,1 casualty=1,999,1,1000,1,1 sector=4,9999,1,1,10000,1 triage=2,9,0,0,0,10 stamp=1700000000000,9999999999999,0,0,0,0 = true,true,false,false,false,false
# A place on the globe, the line frame's tag and the band, from its parts
check waymark.place_ok lat=90000000,-90000000,90000001,0 lon=180000000,-180000000,0,-180000001 = true,true,false,false
# agree: waymark.place_ok each coordinate against its own declared range: Eve and KRON read the same reading the same way
check aerie.frame_tag sync=1 shell=2 trunk=3 = 123
check aerie.frame_tag sync=2 shell=0 trunk=0 = both
check aerie.band_fits bytes=0,512,2048,2049 frame=560,560,2096,2096 = true,true,true,false
check aerie.band_fits bytes=600,600 frame=560,2096 = both
# Where the command post is, a casualty's medical note, and the team room
check watchfire.place_share_ok started=1,1,0 optin=1,0,1 listed=1,1,1 placeok=1,1,1 = true,false,false
check watchfire.place_share_ok started=1,2 optin=1,1 listed=1,1 placeok=1,1 = both
check watchfire.medical_id_ok field=3,6,10 bytes=12,255,1 stamp=1700000000000,1700000000000,0 = true,true,false
check commons.room_post_ok member=1,0,1 joined=1,1,0 enabled=1,1,1 = true,false,false
check commons.room_post_ok member=1,2 joined=1,1 enabled=1,1 = both
